{
  "about": [
    "Real answers of the public RPCs of Base (chain 8453, https://mainnet.base.org) and Base Sepolia (chain 84532, https://sepolia.base.org) to read-only JSON-RPC requests, recorded on 2026-10-14: eth_chainId, eth_getCode at each address below, and eth_call of the Safe's getThreshold() (0xe75235b8) and getOwners() (0xa0e67e2b) at three contracts on Base and one on Base Sepolia, all at the latest block.",
    "Every eth_getCode answer that is not empty is cut to its first 32 bytes; the check asks only whether an address holds code. Nothing else is changed.",
    "On Base: the 0xSplits v2.2 factory, implementation and warehouse, Multicall3 and USDC; Base Sepolia's USDC address, which holds no code there; safe, the Safe that administers the bridged USDbC token on Base (threshold 3 of 6 owners); safeSingleton, the Safe 1.4.1 singleton, which answers getThreshold but not getOwners; feeDisburser, a proxy contract that answers neither; distributor, the Base Sepolia experiment's distributor, which holds no code on Base.",
    "On Base Sepolia: the same contracts with Base Sepolia's USDC; commission, the experiment's commission wallet, which holds no code; and safeSingleton, the Safe 1.4.1 singleton there, which answers getThreshold but not getOwners.",
    "Recorded on 2026-10-15, from the same RPCs: on Base, eth_getCode and the Safe's getThreshold() and getOwners() at commissionSafe, the product owner's Safe 1.5.0 (123 bytes of proxy code, threshold 1, one owner); on Base Sepolia, eth_getCode at testChannelCommission, the test channel's commission wallet, which holds no code."
  ],
